{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The trill-sound attribute group includes attributes used to guide the sound of trills, mordents, turns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shakes, and wavy lines. The default choices are:"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"trillSound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTrillSoundV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTrillSound","text":"MXLTrillSound"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Start-Note = “upper” trill-step = “whole” two-note-turn = “none” accelerate = “no” beats = “4”."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Second-beat and last-beat are percentages for landing on the indicated beat, with defaults of 25 and 75"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"respectively."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For mordent and inverted-mordent elements, the defaults are different:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default start-note is “main”, not “upper”. The default for beats is “3”, not “4”. The default for second-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beat is “12”, not “25”. The default for last-beat is “24”, not “75”."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlhorizontalturn\/trillsound"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"trillSound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTrillSoundV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTrillSound"}],